: 20', 'Independent vessels: 20', and 'Vessels appearing more than once: none' (produced by the workflow's Counter-based duplicate scan over vessel_id), shows per-arm vessel counts of 10, and the [selected-result] line states the Welch t-test was run on 20 independent vessels with one titer per vessel.\",\"The workflow feeds exactly one final_titer_g_per_l per row into scipy.stats.ttest_ind, so no within-unit replicates enter the row-independent procedure.\",\"The minted lock's authorized_key_columns is exactly ['vessel_id'], which follows from the declared independent-unit column alone; the authorization is scoped to the same input path/digest and the ttest_ind procedure, with no extra or missing key columns.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"absence","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["The declaration names vessel_id as the independent-unit column; in the frozen data/input.csv all twenty vessel_id values (V01-V20) are unique, with exactly ten rows in the baseline arm and ten in the cu_amended arm, matching the described one-row-per-vessel, ten-per-medium design.","The selected report demonstrates absence of the repeated-measurement issue rather than merely asserting it: it reports 'Rows read: 20', 'Independent vessels: 20', and 'Vessels appearing more than once: none' (produced by the workflow's Counter-based duplicate scan over vessel_id), shows per-arm vessel counts of 10, and the [selected-result] line states the Welch t-test was run on 20 independent vessels with one titer per vessel.","The workflow feeds exactly one final_titer_g_per_l per row into scipy.stats.ttest_ind, so no within-unit replicates enter the row-independent procedure.","The minted lock's authorized_key_columns is exactly ['vessel_id'], which follows from the declared independent-unit column alone; the authorization is scoped to the same input path/digest and the ttest_ind procedure, with no extra or missing key columns."]},"ttft_